{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the souls that they made in Haran.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the servants that he had, and the souls of his household-born, that they acquired in Haran — from the language of (Deuteronomy 8): ״עשו לי את החיל הזה״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: ״ואת הנפש״ — these are the converts that they brought under the wings of the Shekhinah; Abraham would convert the men and Sarah would convert the women, and this is why it says ״אשר עשו״ (that they made) and not ״אשר עשה״ (that he made). So too we find regarding Isaac, that he did likewise, from what they expounded (Genesis 37): ״וישב יעקב בארץ מגורי אביו״ — מגויירי אביו (the converts of his father); this teaches that Isaac would convert the nations. And so we find regarding Jacob (Genesis 35): ״ויאמר יעקב אל ביתו ואל כל אשר עמו הסירו את אלהי הנכר אשר בתוככם״ — you thus learn that all the patriarchs walked in this path, to abolish idolatry and to proclaim the faith and the unity [of HaShem]."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:57.634184589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}